task.prompt:
Create performant zUI list/table APIs intended for large application datasets such as HTunes music libraries, ZProject task lists, asset browsers, and editor/project trees.

Do not represent thousands of rows as thousands of individually constructed zUI child controls.

Use appropriate native virtualization/owner-data mechanisms for each backend.

The model should conceptually allow the native control to request only the data required for visible rows.

Requirements:
tens of thousands of rows should be practical;
scrolling must not rebuild the screen;
visible rows/items should be reused where possible;
incremental collection updates must be supported;
selection should survive data updates when the key still exists;
columns should support headers, widths, alignment, and sortable metadata;
item identity should be separate from display index;
applications should not need backend-specific WinForms/Win32 code to use virtualization.

Add a benchmark/demo using a large synthetic dataset such as 50,000 rows.

Record baseline performance expectations for creation, scrolling, selection, and incremental updates.
